**What was deleted, and why it's safe to delete:** the manual `checkpointLocation`/`writeStream` wiring (Lakeflow manages it), the explicit quarantine `.filter()`/`saveAsTable()` pair (replaced by `expect_or_drop`, with the same drop behavior), and both `DeltaTable.forName(...).merge(...)` calls (replaced by the `dlt.read_stream()`/`dlt.read()` dependency references, which Lakeflow uses to keep each table correctly updated).

See the downloadable **Unity Catalog Governance Setup Script** below for the complete, runnable version. The core structure:

```sql
USE CATALOG nyc_taxi;

-- Required session privileges
GRANT USE CATALOG ON CATALOG nyc_taxi TO `data-engineers`;
GRANT USE CATALOG ON CATALOG nyc_taxi TO `analytics-team`;
GRANT USE CATALOG ON CATALOG nyc_taxi TO `contractors`;

GRANT USE SCHEMA ON SCHEMA nyc_taxi.bronze TO `data-engineers`;
GRANT USE SCHEMA ON SCHEMA nyc_taxi.silver TO `data-engineers`;
GRANT USE SCHEMA ON SCHEMA nyc_taxi.silver TO `contractors`;
GRANT USE SCHEMA ON SCHEMA nyc_taxi.gold   TO `analytics-team`;

-- Group-appropriate grant width
GRANT SELECT, MODIFY ON SCHEMA nyc_taxi.bronze TO `data-engineers`;
GRANT SELECT, MODIFY ON SCHEMA nyc_taxi.silver TO `data-engineers`;
GRANT SELECT ON SCHEMA nyc_taxi.gold TO `analytics-team`;
GRANT SELECT ON TABLE nyc_taxi.silver.trips TO `contractors`;  -- table-level, deliberately narrower

-- Column mask: VendorID hidden from everyone except data-engineers
CREATE FUNCTION nyc_taxi.silver.mask_vendor_id(vendor_id STRING)
RETURNS STRING
RETURN CASE WHEN is_member('data-engineers') THEN vendor_id ELSE 'REDACTED' END;

ALTER TABLE nyc_taxi.silver.trips ALTER COLUMN VendorID SET MASK nyc_taxi.silver.mask_vendor_id;

-- Row filter: contractors see only their assigned region
CREATE FUNCTION nyc_taxi.silver.filter_by_region(pickup_borough STRING)
RETURNS BOOLEAN
RETURN is_member('data-engineers') OR is_member('analytics-team')
       OR pickup_borough = current_user_region();

ALTER TABLE nyc_taxi.silver.trips SET ROW FILTER nyc_taxi.silver.filter_by_region ON (Borough);
```

